<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Terra-Shore-Read: Lares (Tasked Spirit). Read-only diagnosis. Repo worktree: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt (branch feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5&#45;-b1-lift, head 09ed61bd1; its parent lane head 83ca74cca read GREEN on the full CI). Write nothing. Mark claims MEASURED (file:line) or INFER.
CI (cell web-tw5) reds two cases of packages/lararium-web/tests/e2e/shore-writes.e2e.test.ts: "served wiki saves a draft tiddler without worker errors" and "the vessel page reports its instruments: long animation fra…". The failing log excerpt: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/terra-shore-read/fail-excerpt.log (full: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/ci-42178118605.log). Since 83ca74cca the lane added: the floor broker's vessel:* routes (public/ceremony-broker.js), the vessel host's port:want / port:minted per-follower connect (src/workers/vessel-host.ts), protocol types (src/vessel-protocol.ts, src/ceremony-protocol.ts), tests. Read `git diff 83ca74cca..09ed61bd1 -- packages/lararium-web/src packages/lararium-web/public`.
Find: which change makes the page see a worker error or miss its instruments report (a new message kind the page's handler rejects? a service-worker message the page now receives? a connect() refactor that drops a handler?), with the exact line; or whether the fault predates the lane (the handoff names shore-writes as a load-sensitive test that passes alone — weigh that only after ruling out the diff). Name the minimal cure as an exact file list and change, and the red that must fail first.
Final message under 600 words.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

